          "text": "Let the ball cost **x** dollars.\n\nThe bat costs **$1.00 more**, so the bat costs:\n\n**x + 1.00**\n\nTogether they cost **$1.10**:\n\n**x + (x + 1.00) = 1.10**\n\nCombine terms:\n\n**2x + 1.00 = 1.10**\n\nSubtract 1.00 from both sides:\n\n**2x = 0.10**\n\nDivide by 2:\n\n**x = 0.05**\n\nSo the ball costs **$0.05**, or **5 cents**."
